From: StanleyYP Wang <StanleyYP.Wang@mediatek.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Jul 2023 17:06:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: txpower info, RegDB bypass and LPI

Txpower and regulatory extensions: txpower_info debugfs dump of the
firmware power configuration, device tree single-SKU tables made
authoritative over the kernel regulatory database, and 6 GHz Low
Power Indoor support (LPI_CTRL command, PSD country handling,
beacon/duplicate mode power table selection).

The sku-index node matching in mt76_find_power_limits_node() from
the LPI commit is not carried: no consumer sends a SKU index that
selects a different table. The sku_idx field remains as
vendor-command state only.

Squash of the following MediaTek commits:
- wifi: mt76: mt7915: add txpower info dump support
  (StanleyYP Wang, 2023-07-11)
- wifi: mt76: mt7915: Disable RegDB when enable single sku
  (Allen Ye, 2023-08-11)
- wifi: mt76: mt7915: Add support for lpi and duplicate mode
  (Allen Ye, 2023-12-15)
